"kind":"trace",
"id":"lowbit_walk",
"source":"lowbit_walk.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    data = raw.split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    i = int(data[1])\n    j = int(data[2])\n\n    up = []\n    while i <= n:\n        up.append(i)\n        low = i & -i\n        i += low\n\n    down = []\n    while j > 0:\n        down.append(j)\n        low = j & -j\n        j -= low\n\n    print(\"update visits\", up)\n    print(\"query visits\", down)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program reads an array size, an update position and a query position. The first loop adds the lowest set bit to the position until it passes the size, collecting the positions an update visits. The second loop subtracts the lowest set bit until it reaches 0, collecting the positions a query visits.",
